[38;5;246m⏺ [39mUser answered Claude's questions:
[38;5;246m  ⎿  · Is this app used by one person, or by several people sharing tasks? → Single-user (Recommended)[39m

[38;5;231m⏺[39m Single-user it is. That reshapes the original request, and I want to say so plainly rather than quietly designing
  around it.

  [1mIn a single-user app, you are the only thing that changes tasks.[0m So "notify me when a task changes" mostly means "tell
  me about the edit I just made" — which is noise. The useful triggers in a single-user tool aren't [3mchanges[0m at all;
  they're [1mtime[0m (this is due, this is overdue, this has gone stale) and possibly [3mexternal[0m input (a calendar, an import).
  That's a different engine: a scheduler over task metadata, not an event bus over mutations.

  Which means my earlier advice to build layer 3 as an event log is now wrong for your case — drop it. Events buy you
  almost nothing when there's one actor. Due dates and a check-on-load are far simpler and cover the real need.

  So before I design anything:
